This directory holds the original XQuest v1.3 game data files required
to build and run xquest-sdl.

The data files are NOT stored in git (they are gitignored) because they
are copyrighted by Mark Mackey and carry a custom freeware licence that
does not permit redistribution as part of a source repository.

To populate this directory, run:

    scripts/fetch-assets.sh

That script copies the required files from the adjacent ../xquest/
directory (the original DOS source/binary distribution).

Required files
--------------
  xquest.gfx   — all sprites (ship, enemies, objects, fonts, gates)
  xquest.enm   — binary enemy definitions
  xquest.fnt   — game font
  xquest.snd   — raw 8-bit 11025 Hz mono PCM sound effects
  startpic.pbm — title-screen planar bitmap (convert_pbm.py produces .raw)

Optional but useful
-------------------
  xquest.scr   — initial empty high-score table (created by game if absent)
  xquest.cfg   — default configuration (created by game if absent)

The original XQuest distribution can be downloaded from various freeware
archives; search for "XQuest 1.3 Mark Mackey".
